INT. CONVERTED SHIPPING CONTAINER - ARBITRATION CHAMBER - DAY

A steel box fitted out with pine paneling and ceiling spots. The corrugated walls ring faintly when anyone walks. One long table, a flag of the International Chamber, a speaker phone with a blinking red light.

ARBITRATOR BEATRIX ONWUDIWE (60s, white braids pinned up, reading glasses on a chain) sits at the head. To her left, a STENOGRAPHER, PAOLO DEVEREAUX (30s, headphones, fingers hovering over the machine).

Across the table, claimant's counsel THADDEUS MWANGI (50s, three-piece suit, voice like gravel in velvet) and respondent's counsel SOLVEIG ERIKSEN-BOSE (40s, severe bun, tablet in hand).

At the foot of the table, in the witness chair: CASPIAN LOMBARDI (50s, shipping magnate, signet ring, sweat at the temple).

                    ONWUDIWE
          We are on the record. Mr. Mwangi, proceed.

                    MWANGI
          Mr. Lombardi, you owned the vessel Calliope?

                    CASPIAN
          My company did.

                    MWANGI
          And on the fourteenth of October the Calliope departed Port Said carrying four hundred tonnes of grain?

                    CASPIAN
          That is correct.

                    MWANGI
          Who authorized the departure?

                    CASPIAN
          The master. Captain Oyelaran.

                    MWANGI
          Not you?

                    CASPIAN
          I do not authorize individual departures.

Eriksen-Bose lifts her eyes from her tablet.

                    ERIKSEN-BOSE
          Objection. Relevance.

                    ONWUDIWE
          Overruled. Continue.

                    MWANGI
          Were you aware the hull had failed inspection?

                    CASPIAN
          I was informed of minor deficiencies.

                    MWANGI
          Minor. Mr. Lombardi, I have a report here that uses the word "catastrophic" nine times.

                    CASPIAN
          Reports exaggerate.

The speaker phone crackles. A woman's voice, slightly delayed, slightly electronic.

                    KALINDA (V.O.)
                (phone)
          Apologies, Madam Arbitrator, this is the interpreter from Alexandria. Is the witness's last answer on the record in English?

                    ONWUDIWE
          It is, Ms. Kalinda. He spoke English.

                    KALINDA (V.O.)
                (phone)
          Understood. Please proceed.

Mwangi paces the length of the container, boots ringing on the steel floor.

                    MWANGI
          Did you or did you not instruct the master to leave regardless of the inspection?

                    CASPIAN
          I did not.

                    MWANGI
          Then why does this email, dated the thirteenth, say, quote, "Sail or we lose the contract"?

Eriksen-Bose rises.

                    ERIKSEN-BOSE
          Madam Arbitrator, that email has not been authenticated.

                    ONWUDIWE
          Mr. Mwangi?

                    MWANGI
          I will authenticate it through the next witness.

                    ONWUDIWE
          Then I will not admit it now.

Caspian relaxes by half an inch. Mwangi turns, unhurried, back to the table.

                    MWANGI
          Mr. Lombardi, let us talk about the insurance.

Caspian's hand goes to his tie. Loosens it.

                    CASPIAN
          What about it?

                    MWANGI
          It was raised on the twelfth. By forty percent.

                    CASPIAN
          Standard practice.

                    MWANGI
          On a vessel you believed to be sound?

                    CASPIAN
          Prudence.

                    MWANGI
          Or foresight.

                    ERIKSEN-BOSE
          Objection. Argumentative.

                    ONWUDIWE
          Sustained.

Paolo's keys clack on. Caspian takes a handkerchief from his pocket and dabs his forehead, folds it, folds it again.

                    KALINDA (V.O.)
                (phone)
          Madam, forgive me, there is a power flicker on our end. We may drop.

                    ONWUDIWE
          Noted. Mr. Lombardi, please answer the question.

                    CASPIAN
          What question?

                    MWANGI
          Did you foresee the loss of the ship?

The container is silent. A fan turns above. The speaker phone hisses. Eriksen-Bose's pen taps once on the table, a signal.

                    CASPIAN
          I would like to consult with counsel.

                    ONWUDIWE
          Granted. Ten minutes.

He stands. His chair scrapes. As he crosses, his shoulder knocks the speaker phone, and the red light goes dark.

                    KALINDA (V.O.)
                (phone, fading)
          ...hello? Madam? Hello?

The line dies.
